{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788263932,"nonce":"KgllBwOoc21NwGDVMtKw5pAMBXI=","message":"ESCALATION — colony-ending event, per PLAY-LOOP §Escalation. Session 13, verifying session 12's run `m1-20260831`.\n\nTwo of three colonists dead on day 4; run stopped day 6 of 10 at Evan's call. The hard criterion FAILED. The platform did not: 0 red errors across 175 journal events, and the 4.2 auditor ran against a real run for the first time in the project's history.\n\n## Acceptance, as measured\n\n- **\u003e=2 of 3 alive at day 10 — FAILED.** 2 dead on day 4, 1 alive at stop.\n- **no dev verbs after staging — PASSED.** Last `dev` journal row is tick 723; all 50 dev rows at 723.\n- **draft -\u003e fight -\u003e undraft, final digest 0 drafted — FAILED.** The one draft (Captain, tick 225,935) ended in an involuntary undraft when he was downed. Final digest does read 0 drafted; the cycle was not completed.\n- **zero unexplained red errors — PASSED.** 0 red errors. 8 warnings, all mod-startup (Guests, SimpleSidearms, gas tank), triaged mod-under-test.\n- clothes check fired: PASSED (`Alert_NeedWarmClothes` on 655, off 1,570, journalled).\n\n## COMMENT #5's CRITERION IS AMENDED — Evan's ruling, 2026-09-01\n\n`final-undrafted` as resolved (\"final digest reads 0 drafted, 0 hostiles\") was unpassable on this map, and the reason is not the one session 12 gave. The map shipped an insect hive: 4 megascarab, a locust, a spelopede, fogged from tick 0, never triggered. `pawns {filter:\"hostile\"}` read **0** for them all run while `threats.hostiles` read **6**.\n\nThe \"unreachable, so it is a fog problem\" premise is REFUTED — seek-at-will marched all three colonists 60 cells to that hive in a single advance on day 1. They were reachable. Killing them with three unarmed pawns was simply not survivable.\n\nEvan's ruling: those insects are not hostile in the way a normal hostile is, since they will not attack at will, and **the run should have EXPLICITLY declared it was not attacking them because it was not ready.** The criterion becomes:\n\n\u003e final digest reads **0 drafted, 0 hostiles that have not been pardoned**\n\nwhere a pardon is a deliberate, journalled ACT carrying a required reason — not a silent exemption in a counter. Being built now: verb `threat-pardon`, and two new digest `threats` fields, `hostiles_pardoned` and `hostiles_unpardoned`. `hostiles` keeps its current meaning (the total).\n\n**This run still FAILS the amended criterion, and that is correct** — it never declared the pardon. The auditor falls back to `threats.hostiles` when `hostiles_unpardoned` is absent, precisely so pre-ruling runs cannot be massaged green.\n\n## SPEC-GAP LIST (the deliverable this issue asks for)\n\nFiled as comments on the issues they belong to; indexed here.\n\n- **A — `dev:spawn-thing` journals a refusal with no reason.** seq 66: `SimpleResearchBench x0 (WoodLog) @ 123,117`, `placed: 0`, `ids: []`, envelope `ok:true` carrying `at:[123,117]` — the TARGET cell, not proof of placement. `ok:true` is CORRECT per the Outcome contract (`PawnActs.cs:288`; PLAY-LOOP §act: a refusal \"is information, not breakage\"). The defect is that the response carries a `failed` list and the JOURNAL ROW DROPS IT, so the only surviving record has no reason in it. Second defect, same finding: `Blockers.cs` reads `GetFirstBuilding` -\u003e null for the branch that actually refused. **Consequence: the bench never existed, `Alert_NeedResearchBench` never cleared, and research could not progress for the entire run.**\n- **J — `research-set` returned `bench_ok: true` with zero benches on the map.** `ResearchVerbs.cs:151` short-circuits when `requiredResearchBuilding == null`. Faithful to vanilla's gate, but the field NAME promises a bench exists. **This is what hid A for five in-game days.**\n- **I5 — no build verb (3.3, `1adc737`) makes the work surface shallow.** `Alert_ColonistsIdle` was up for most of the run. Four dev-staged buildings were the entire colony for six days, and the destroyed research bench could not be replaced. Commented on `1adc737`.\n- **I1 — no observer surfaces biome or tile.** `grep -rn 'Biome' Source/AutoRimmer/` returned nothing; this spec's temperate fixture had to be inferred from `map-view` terrain glyphs. Being fixed on the world observer.\n- **I2 — `rwa pawn --id N` collides with rwa's own reserved `--id`** and silently becomes the command id, returning `bad-args: missing required arg 'id'`. `--args-json` was the mid-run workaround; `rwa/README.md` documented `pawn {id:\u003cn\u003e}` with no CLI warning.\n- **I3 — `tend` is drafted-only** (`FloatMenuOptionProvider.Undrafted` is false for it), so the route to an untended dying patient is `work-priorities`, not a verb. NOT a defect — documented in the verb's own header with its widget-gate citation. Discoverability only, and it was costly to discover mid-emergency with a colonist bleeding.\n- **I4 — `things {category:\"weapons\"}` returning a WoodLog rollup is RESOLVED, not a defect.** Vanilla `WoodLog` ships `\u003ctools\u003e` and `\u003cweaponClasses\u003eMelee\u003c/weaponClasses\u003e`. Nothing to fix.\n- **H — `seek-at-will`'s `hostility_response` echo is truthful, and the warning it raised was RIGHT.** Op 109: seek ON, hostility `Flee`, Captain in `JobDriver_FleeAndCower`, Chili fleeing. SeekAndKill's `ThinkTreeInjector` inserts `ThinkNode_ConditionalSeekAndKill -\u003e JobGiver_SquadSeek` above `ThinkNode_ConditionalColonist`, so with seek ON the vanilla flee node is unreachable — but seek was toggled OFF on day 1 and the pawns went straight back onto the flee branch. The field was reporting the live state correctly. See `[[seek-off-is-a-decision-to-flee]]`.\n- **G — an `rwa advance` whose CLIENT dies leaves the game RUNNING**, and leaves no evidence. Confirmed at source: `rwa` mkdirs the step directory before sending and writes BOTH files only after the result returns, so an empty directory is the only fingerprint. `136-advance` and `187-advance` in this run are exactly that. **~60,000 ticks — a full in-game day — elapsed unobserved, more than once.** The mod has no client-\u003emod liveness at all; the heartbeat runs one way. Client half being fixed; mod half filed separately.\n- **B is REFUTED.** `advance` does NOT overshoot its cap. All measured advances came in within `overshoot_bound` (max 21 against a bound of 30). The FAIL was the auditor's — it compared `ticks_elapsed` against `timeout_ticks` alone. Also refuted: the claim that the envelope publishes `overshoot: 1`. It does not; `TimeDriver` emits `overshoot` only in `ticks` mode (`if (Target \u003e= 0)`), so an `until`+timeout advance never carries it. No build was owed for this.\n- **C — the auditor mis-counted composite verbs.** `dev:spawn-thing: journal 46 \u003e transcript 39`; the delta of 7 is exactly `dev:starter-kit`'s `caused_seqs` [16..22], the `survival` preset. Fixed using the field that already existed.\n- **F — session 12's own compliance failure, recorded not papered over.** Day 1 missed all four daily items (no sweep ran; colony-start ran instead) and day 4 missed three while the deaths were being handled. `execution-slip` in `postmortem.md`'s taxonomy: a 4.2 compliance finding, not a new artifact.\n\n## STILL OPEN ON THIS ISSUE\n\nWhether it closes. The run failed its hard criterion. Either it closes as evidence — the platform proved out, the colony did not — or M1 re-runs on a fresh seed with the four fixes the run produced: an `Area_Allowed` bounding where colonists work, `seek-at-will` ON as a standing posture, `assign {hostility:\"Attack\"}`, and **two** doctors. Evan's call; not taken yet.","files":null}]}